  "summary": "The app renders a candy-red car on a slowly rotating turntable in a dark showroom, and it typechecks and builds. I did not build the faint mirrored reflection of the car on the platform. The platform top is instead polished and picks up the studio highlights.\n\n- **Scene content:** `recipes/carpaint.mjs` builds the car, imported with `import_three` into `src/three-bridge/carpaint.*` (the `.bridge.ts` file is generated; I did not touch `carpaint.scene.ts`, which `main.ts` doesn't use). The car has a smooth body, a dark glass cabin with a red roof, a chrome belt line and window trim, and four dark rubber wheels with chrome rims. The platform has a chrome edge, a glowing ring light and tick marks.\n- **Paint:** the candy-red base has a fine flake normal map generated in code, under a clearcoat layer.\n- **Lighting and camera (`src/main.ts`):** a studio \"softbox\" environment, three rect-area strip lights (two overhead, one at the side) and a faint cool rim light. The camera stays fixed at a low front-three-quarter angle with the whole object in frame.\n- **Turntable:** the platform and car rotate at 20°/s. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame with the increasing `turntableAngleDeg` and `paintFinish: 'clearcoat'`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n- **Mirror:** a planar mirror on the platform only showed the car's dark underside as a black square, so I removed it.\n\nThe roof cap floats slightly above the glass in the last screenshot."
